  "title": "Unified Title",
  "summary": "ThinkWorld bridges human vision-language reasoning with world dynamics through Chain-of-Dynamics (CoD) sequences, while PDRVLA leverages physical tokens from video-world models to condition action generation. Both models address challenges in VLA understanding and generalization.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "ThinkWorld represents each action thought as a Chain-of-Dynamics (CoD), a sequence of discrete motion tokens that captures the intermediate dynamics connecting the current world to a future state.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "PDRVLA uses a lightweight Physical Dynamics Module to extract physical tokens from vision-language features, enabling action generation without online video generation.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Experiments show PDRVLA achieves high success rates on four simulation benchmarks, with improvements in future prediction and subtask conditioning.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
